{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Give thanks to YHWH, for He is good</b> — the word הוא is elided. The meaning is: for He is good." "And some say: כי טוב — a singular past verb, in the manner of מה טובו אהליך [how goodly are your tents], which is a plural past verb."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:54.850758907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}